    {
      "sha": "a069247ca8e1f89be44863932a452028ecee4078",
      "node_id": "C_kwDOUIOGatoAKGEwNjkyNDdjYThlMWY4OWJlNDQ4NjM5MzJhNDUyMDI4ZWNlZTQwNzg",
      "commit": {
        "author": {
          "name": "Dillon Dupont",
          "email": "dillon@trycua.com",
          "date": "2026-10-03T11:23:13Z"
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Dillon Dupont",
          "email": "dillon@trycua.com",
          "date": "2026-10-03T11:23:13Z"
        },
        "message": "fix(cua-driver): drain foreground input before restoring the previous window\n\nForeground type_text/press_key restored the prior foreground window a\nfixed 40 ms after SendInput. Editors that process Return slowly had not\nconsumed the queued tail yet, so text after a line break was dropped or\ndelivered elsewhere. Attach to the foreground thread's input queue\nbefore inserting, append an unassigned-VK sentinel, and restore only\nafter the target thread has read it (bounded at 2 s).\n\nReplaces the batching/admission changes on this branch (an A/B on the\nnative Windows lane showed batching alone does not change delivery) and\nreverts the generated type_text reference accordingly; keeps the\nWPF/WinUI3 multiline fixtures, app-owned oracle and tests, with the\nresponse assertion updated to the current route contract.\n\nFixes #4477\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Hv7NU2xZDx8fqykTXiaDuj",
        "tree": {
          "sha": "e4c4d2f3fec1c3f8dbca3e673c1d4277fca2ca69",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/trycua/cua/git/trees/e4c4d2f3fec1c3f8dbca3e673c1d4277fca2ca69"
